{"attachment": {"content": "- worldlabs:atlas-blender: Use Blender to see and shape Atlas scenes in 3D. Load posed images as cameras and point clouds, place cameras by eye, animate a camera path, view splats, and optionally run Atlas tasks from inside Blender with the Atlas add-on. Use when Blender is installed or the user works in Blender.\n- worldlabs:atlas-flythrough: Make a camera-move video through a scene (flythrough, walkthrough, orbit, push-in, pan) from one or more photos or a generated image with World Labs Atlas. Use when the user wants a video or a camera move from images, or new angles of a scene that may become one.\n- worldlabs:atlas-splats: Turn one or more photos or a generated image into a 3D scene as Gaussian splats (an SPZ file) with World Labs Atlas. Use when the user wants a 3D scene, a world to explore, splats, or a scene to view, export or mesh from images, or new angles and views of a place from an image.\n- worldlabs:worldlabs-cli: Run World Labs Atlas API tasks from a terminal with the worldlabs CLI. Covers install and sign-in, uploading files, running a task from a JSON request, waiting for it, and downloading its outputs. Use for any Atlas job without a skill of its own, such as generating or editing an image, estimating camera and depth, or extracting a mesh, and for CLI setup and errors. New views of a scene belong to atlas-splats or atlas-flythrough. Also covers the connected World Labs tools when there is no shell.", "digests": ["7b1e2f528d0f93b0", "60ac7cd1d57d57ba", "d0638fbbb6ac059d", "6159a336d356a076"], "isInitial": false, "names": ["worldlabs:atlas-blender", "worldlabs:atlas-flythrough", "worldlabs:atlas-splats", "worldlabs:worldlabs-cli"], "skillCount": 4, "type": "skill_listing"}, "cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "ccr-61131b9d-uj0oqb", "isSidechain": false, "parentUuid": "29af2215-c440-45ec-bcdd-dda17359d84d", "rendered": [{"content": "<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are available for use with the Skill tool:\n\n- worldlabs:atlas-blender: Use Blender to see and shape Atlas scenes in 3D. Load posed images as cameras and point clouds, place cameras by eye, animate a camera path, view splats, and optionally run Atlas tasks from inside Blender with the Atlas add-on. Use when Blender is installed or the user works in Blender.\n- worldlabs:atlas-flythrough: Make a camera-move video through a scene (flythrough, walkthrough, orbit, push-in, pan) from one or more photos or a generated image with World Labs Atlas. Use when the user wants a video or a camera move from images, or new angles of a scene that may become one.\n- worldlabs:atlas-splats: Turn one or more photos or a generated image into a 3D scene as Gaussian splats (an SPZ file) with World Labs Atlas. Use when the user wants a 3D scene, a world to explore, splats, or a scene to view, export or mesh from images, or new angles and views of a place from an image.\n- worldlabs:worldlabs-cli: Run World Labs Atlas API tasks from a terminal with the worldlabs CLI. Covers install and sign-in, uploading files, running a task from a JSON request, waiting for it, and downloading its outputs. Use for any Atlas job without a skill of its own, such as generating or editing an image, estimating camera and depth, or extracting a mesh, and for CLI setup and errors. New views of a scene belong to atlas-splats or atlas-flythrough. Also covers the connected World Labs tools when there is no shell.\n</system-reminder>"}], "renderedRole": "system", "sessionId": "e47fc047-26b4-5efa-bfda-db0784968866", "timestamp": "2026-11-16T22:12:22.831Z", "type": "attachment", "userType": "external", "uuid": "965a32af-3395-4065-8148-a0083b3a50d7", "version": "2.1.325"}
{"attachment": {"changed": true, "files": [{"content": "# RAINBOW — permanent rules for Claude Code\n\nThis is an EXISTING, playable 11-screen 3D game. **Never restart it, never start from scratch, never delete work.**\n\n## 1. Every new session or new Claude account — recovery is automatic\nThe SessionStart hook (`.claude/settings.json` → `scripts/autosave-hook.sh` → **`scripts/claude-bootstrap.sh --hook`**)\nalready ran before your first turn: it fetched every branch, merged any newer `ccr-*`/`claude/*` branch (normal merges\nonly; a conflicting merge is aborted and reported), restored the Git LFS binaries, re-armed the five-minute autosave and\nstarted the full bootstrap in the background. Its summary (\"RAINBOW SESSION START\") is in your context.\n1. `bash scripts/claude-bootstrap.sh --status` → `backups/BOOTSTRAP_REPORT.md` (re-run when it says \"still in progress\").\n   No summary in context, or an old checkout? Run `bash scripts/claude-bootstrap.sh` yourself; from a branch without it:\n   `git fetch origin claude/rainbow-05-water-projection && git show FETCH_HEAD:scripts/claude-bootstrap.sh > /tmp/b.sh && bash /tmp/b.sh`.\n   (Legacy prompts call `scripts/resume-newest-work.sh --tools`; it runs the bootstrap.)\n2. Read `backups/CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_TRANSFER.md` (top section only), `backups/AGENTS_STATUS.json`,\n   `backups/TOOL_MANIFEST.json` and the current briefs: **`qa/pilot05/proj/`** (water texture projection — `NOTES.md` when it\n   exists, `BRIEF_SPECIALIST1_VERBATIM.md`, `BRIEF_SPECIALIST2.md`), `qa/pilot05/wave12/NOTES.md`, `qa/pilot05/COORDINATION_WAVE9B.md`.\n3. Check connectors yourself (ToolSearch `World_Labs_Atlas`, `github`, `playwright`) and give the user the backup\n   report of §4. Tell the user plainly about every failure and every backup GAP the bootstrap reports.\nThe GitHub default branch is an OLD version. Newest work as of 2026-11-16 ~16:00 UTC: branch\n**`claude/rainbow-05-water-projection`** (the Screen 05 water-projection experiment; contains every other `ccr-*` /\n`claude/*` branch). `ccr-451ea8c7-3nqlis` (`97dda28`) = the user's current WORKING version (T2 default + W12 candidates),\nprotected. `codex/*` branches hold Codex's separate water experiment: preserved, protected, **never merge them\nautomatically** (the bootstrap only merges `ccr-*` / `claude/*`). The bootstrap's merge result always wins over this line. Ready-to-paste prompt for a\nnew account: `backups/START_NEW_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT.md`. The bootstrap checks before installing (Blender 5.3.0, Android SDK\n34, npm, Python libs, World Labs plugin): never reinstall a working tool by hand, never run `playwright install`.\n\n## 2. Five-minute GitHub autosave — the user's standing order (2026-11-15/16), never ask about routine saves\n* `scripts/rainbow-autosave.py` runs every 5 minutes while the cloud environment is active (loop daemon\n  `scripts/autosave-daemon.sh`, re-armed by the SessionStart and Stop hooks) plus on PreCompact / Stop / SessionEnd.\n  It commits all allow-listed project files (code, unfinished specialist edits, screenshots, Marble and Blender files,\n  docs), pushes to THIS session's own `ccr-*`/`claude/*` branch, verifies remote SHA == local HEAD and logs every run\n  in `backups/BACKUP_LOG.md` (+ `backups/.live/`). A lock prevents simultaneous saves and races with merges / LFS.\n* NEVER force-push, reset, rebase, rewrite history or push to `protected_branches` in `backups/autosave.config.json`\n  (`ccr-6f431adf-7h0m8y` original, `claude/rainbow-3d-recovery-m4v347` recovery, and every finished earlier session\n  branch). Keep unfinished experiments as URL-switch tests or patches on the session branch, never on protected ones.\n* At session start and after every major task: `python3 -I scripts/autosave-status.py` (expect `AUTOSAVE OK … (match)`).\n  Before ending a session: `python3 scripts/rainbow-autosave.py --reason manual:end`, then confirm\n  `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/<branch>` == `git rev-parse HEAD`.\n* Backups c